# Generic core, concrete feel

Kumkaj is one **business operating system** for **any entity** (shop, service, agency, personal/household books, multi-branch org). Implement **generic primitives**; let labels, config, and progressive enablement make the product feel concrete to that user.

Canonical product text: `docs/KUMKAJ_PRODUCT_VISION_AND_REQUIREMENTS.md` §1–2 and §31–32.

## Do

- Prefer shared primitives: party, item/line, unit, charge, ledger, day book, report view, document template.
- When a client asks for a vertical (“courier parties”, “kg credit”), extract the shared capability and implement that.
- Hide unused capability; do not rename the whole product into one trade.

## Do not

- Hard-code verticals or entity-type product forks (`CourierShipment`, `BarberChair`, “Personal Finance mode”).
- Add trade-specific schemas that duplicate the core.

```text
❌ CourierOutstandingTable / PersonalBudgetAppMode
✅ Party ledger + qty units + day/party reports (owner names parties/units)
```
